Yeah, I wasn't looking for a "we should change lojban suck that..." sort of
thing.  I assumed there was some solution.

Just kind of sucks that it's very easy for me to say "I am looking for a
green thing in my dresser" (mi sisku lo (ka?) crino lo seldacru).  But for
"I'm looking for my keys", I've either got to spend half the day spelling
it all out, or I guess selkik's tanru works  tolerably well "mi troci co
zvafa'i lo mi ckiku"

I guess it just seems like an unfortunate definition for sisku given how
easy it is to *add* an object-by-property aspect to the searching.  i.e.
 "mi sisku lo creka poi crino" or even "mi sisku lo crino creka".

meh, it is what it is.

